Add a USB-gadget variant DTB for the Radxa Cubie A5E

The board's USB-C port is its only OTG-capable port, and sun55i-a523.dtsi
routes BOTH the MUSB peripheral controller (usb_otg) and the ehci0/ohci0 host
controllers to usbphy index 0. The board DTS enables all of them, and the
board has no ID or VBUS detection wired up to arbitrate between them -- its
own DTS says so:

    The schematic describes USB0_ID (PL10), measuring VBUS_5V, which looks to
    be always on. ... The AXP717C provides proper USB-C CC pin functionality,
    but the PMIC is not connected to those pins of the USB-C connector.

With no arbitration, probe order decides, and ehci0 wins on every boot:

    phy phy-4100400.phy.0: Changing dr_mode to 1     <- USB_DR_MODE_HOST
    ehci-platform 4101000.usb: EHCI Host Controller

so dr_mode="peripheral" never takes effect and the port cannot enumerate as a
device (bench-proven on a 1GB board, bean gosd-3io0).

Host and peripheral are therefore mutually exclusive on this hardware and the
choice has to be made at build time. Rather than change the stock DTB -- which
would silently remove USB-C host support from every image, including for the
GPIO-5V-powered setup the stock DTS explicitly caters for -- add a variant DTB
that disables the two host controllers contending for phy 0. GoSD ships the
stock DTB by default and this one only when `gosd build --usb-gadget` asks for
peripheral mode.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e-gadget.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0+ OR MIT)
+/*
+ * Radxa Cubie A5E, USB-gadget variant.
+ *
+ * Identical to the stock board DTB except that the ehci0/ohci0 host
+ * controllers are disabled. Those two share usbphy port 0 with usb_otg
+ * (MUSB), and this board has no ID/VBUS detection to arbitrate between
+ * them, so whichever driver probes last owns the port -- in practice
+ * ehci0, which switches the phy to host mode and leaves the gadget
+ * unable to enumerate however dr_mode is set.
+ *
+ * Disabling them leaves phy 0 to MUSB, which is what dr_mode="peripheral"
+ * in the stock DTS already asks for. The cost is that the USB-C port
+ * cannot act as a USB host in this configuration; the USB 3.0 Type-A
+ * port is unaffected, being wired to ehci1/ohci1.
+ */
+
+#include "sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dts"
+
+&ehci0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&ohci0 {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/Makefile
@@ -56,6 +56,7 @@
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-plus.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-sp.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-a527-cubie-a5e-gadget.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-h728-x96qpro+.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-avaota-a1.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_SUNXI) += sun55i-t527-orangepi-4a.dtb
